plugin-hostd (0.20.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: read same-pass without a ref-pinned checkout
  * release: plugin-hostd-full releases later in this same pass (#125)
  * release: same-pass from a same_pass input or a tracked file at the built
    commit (#125)
  * test: drop the two plugin-hostd-full checks the merge listed again
  * tests: four verbs declared ahead of the daemon, answered from 0.20.8
  * fuzz: the answer-fits-one-line record changes the recorder's bound
  * fuzz: a record changes a file of the tree, never an installed header (red)
  * packaging: plugin-hostd-full and python3-plugin-hostd-protocol leave
    plugin-hostd (green)
  * tests: plugin-hostd builds no plugin-hostd-full and no
    python3-plugin-hostd-protocol (red)
  * tests: rendered_at_tag runs with no .git present and no git
  * check-rendered: a package build judges the render at the renderer it
    recorded
  * tests: a release build judges its render at the renderer the tag recorded
    (red)
  * tests: the CLAP default is the list plugin-hostd-protocol declares,
    ~/.clap then /usr/lib/clap first
  * docs: the guide's clap_path default is plugin-hostd-protocol 0.5.9's five
    folders (make gen)
  * tests: the CLAP default is the list plugin-hostd-protocol declares,
    ~/.clap then /usr/lib/clap first
  * fuzz: the seed corpus holds node_label
  * fuzz: the pin_set record names the line of pin_words.c it changes
  * fuzz: each check's mutant and input records sit in its own comment
  * Artifact retention: explicit retention-days, 30 on a tag and 2 otherwise
  * bench: the smoke job's container gets a /dev/shm large enough for jackd
  * bench/report: the facts cite the zynthian issues under Open-Mixer
  * tools: bounded-install reads a process's stat quietly when it ends
    mid-scan (#81)
  * tools: bounded-install ends a silent attempt only when it is also still
    (#81)
  * tests: an attempt silent but busy is waited for, one silent and still is
    ended, red (#81)
  * tests: the lock holder's stub counts a running process, not an unreaped
    one (#81)
  * tools: bounded-install ends the dpkg an ended apt attempt leaves holding
    the lock (#81)
  * tests: a dpkg that outlives its ended apt attempt is ended before the
    next (red, #81)
  * commit-msg: take the current stub from the checker's release line
  * bench: RSS and PSS from one walk of the process's memory
  * bench: RSS and PSS come from one walk of the process's memory (red)
  * packaging: 0.20.7 floors at the chain line's needs, with their ceilings
  * tools: bounded-install bounds an attempt by inactivity, with a generous
    total (ruling on #81)
  * tests: an install is bounded by inactivity, never a short total: a slow
    one that prints passes (red)
  * tools: bounded-install finishes dpkg's work between apt attempts
  * tests: an apt attempt killed by its timeout is followed by dpkg
    --configure -a before the next (red)
  * ci: every package manager call runs bounded, a hung mirror a fast red
    naming it
  * tests: a timing proof reads the load: it warns on a loaded node and fails
    on a quiet one
  * tools: bounded-install.sh, a package manager's command bounded in CI
  * tests: every package manager step in CI is bounded, a hung mirror a fast
    red naming it (red)
  * test: a timing proof reads the load: warns on a loaded node, fails on a
    quiet one (red)
  * clients: sentence() reads a catalog through omx-contract's catalog
    reader, the entry's text whatever its shape (#78)
  * tests: a catalog entry reads as its text in both clients, whatever its
    shape (red, #78)
  * packaging: plugin-hostd-protocol >= 0.5.8, the first table whose reply
    codes carry transient
  * clients: the fixtures name reply -104 as plugin-hostd-protocol 0.5.8's
    table does
  * bench: the debs job installs lintian, which the shared deb-deps action
    runs on what it builds
  * bench: the smoke run installs the plugin-hostd DEBs its own run built,
    the channel only for the rest
  * tests: bench.yml's smoke run installs the daemon its own run built, like
    every workflow (red)
  * release 0.20.7: build against omx-contract 3.18.0, whose render the
    headers are; bookworm on a full pass only (D30, D25)
  * release 0.20.7: the version in the daemon, the man pages and the
    TypeScript client
  * release 0.20.7: the changelog names what main gained since the release
    was first prepared
  * include: the rendered vocabulary as omx-contract 3.18.0 renders it
  * include: the vocabulary header rendered by omx-contract 3.18.0
  * grouping: the rendered C vocabulary carries the new retry group item (#67)
  * grouping: each reason declares its retry property in grouping.json and
